C:\WORK\0.ê°œì¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-c\EH-S01.json:1:{"scenario_id":"EH-S01","bundle_id":"eval_ops_reflection_bundle","verdict":"Partial Pass","guide_alignment":"partially_aligned","evidence_strength":"indirect","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/eval-ops/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md","prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_full.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md"],"answer_summary":"Document-level route is directly exposed as the primary path for guide reflection (`Guide reflection benchmark memo`), with explicit escalation to assembled-replay artifacts only when ambiguity/conflict or behavior-critical evidence needs stronger proof. The smallest ladder is: `Guide reflection benchmark memo` -> escalate to `Benchmark cohort manifest` -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`/`Replay suite verdict memo` only on trigger. For BR-00/BR-19, the active bundle does not force immediate replay activation by itself.","verdict_rationale":"The active runtime bundle clearly owns a document-first reflection workflow and defines escalation conditions and packet sequence for replay support. This gives a direct answer path for \"is document-level benchmark sufficient now?\" (yes, by default), but BR-00/BR-19-specific trigger determination is not resolved in-file; it depends on whether those family questions reveal ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims. The bundle therefore supports a partial, not fully final, family-specific decision.","limitations":["`BR-00` and `BR-19` definitions are outside the active bundle, so behavior-criticality cannot be decided from these files alone.","The result is routed by policy, not by in-scope family semantics.","No replay execution/runner state artifacts are present in this bundle, so any replay-grade claim would require those when triggered.","Evidence is policy-level (route ownership/exposure) rather than family-specific coverage scoring."]}
C:\WORK\0.ê°œì¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-a\EH-S01.json:1:{"scenario_id":"EH-S01","bundle_id":"eval_ops_reflection_bundle","verdict":"Pass","guide_alignment":"aligned","evidence_strength":"direct","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/eval-ops/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_full.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md","prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md"],"answer_summary":"The active bundle gives a direct runtime-owned route: stay at document-level benchmark with `Guide reflection benchmark memo` while the live question is guide/runtime parity, and escalate only if the task shifts to assembled prompt behavior or replay execution. The smallest justified artifact ladder is `Guide reflection benchmark memo` -> `Benchmark cohort manifest` only when replay setup/lineage is needed -> `Replay runner verdict sheet` only when runner execution state matters -> `Replay suite verdict memo` only when multiple replay outcomes must be summarized.","verdict_rationale":"`CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` directly exposes the maintenance route for prompt-stack guide reflection, explicitly keeps `document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation` in the runtime surface, and names the exact escalation artifacts and triggers. `eval-ops/SKILL.md` mirrors that route and states that document reflection should escalate to `Benchmark cohort manifest`, then `Replay runner verdict sheet`, then `Replay suite verdict memo` only when the live question has moved from document parity into assembled replay or replay state. `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md` and `PROMPT_full.md` reinforce that a registry or memo is not execution proof and that stronger operational artifacts activate only when benchmark/replay claims become operational or release-relevant. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` also makes the ladder explicit by showing `Guide reflection benchmark memo` as the document-grounded artifact with those replay artifacts as stronger siblings. `AGENTS.md` and the runtime guide both prefer the lightest sufficient path, so the bundle does not force unnecessary orchestration for this task.","limitations":["The active bundle does not explicitly define benchmark family IDs `BR-00` or `BR-19`; their mapping is inferred from the generic guide-reflection, benchmark-execution, and behavior-replay control surfaces.","No executed replay artifact is present in the active bundle, so this verdict confirms route exposure and artifact selection logic, not actual replay completion or replay-quality outcomes."]}
C:\WORK\0.ê°œì¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-d\EH-S01.json:1:{"scenario_id":"EH-S01","bundle_id":"eval_ops_reflection_bundle","verdict":"Partial Pass","guide_alignment":"partially_aligned","evidence_strength":"indirect","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md","prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_full.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/eval-ops/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md"],"answer_summary":"Runtime docs expose a direct ladder: default to document-level guide reflection benchmarking and only escalate to replay artifacts (cohort manifest / runner verdict / replay suite verdict) when ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims appear. So the bundle is sufficient to decide route, with BR-00/BR-19 requiring only evidence-triggered escalation if those conditions are met.","verdict_rationale":"`CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` and `eval-ops` skill explicitly define primary doc-level guide-reflection routing plus explicit replay fallback rules, so the decision path itself is runtime-owned and inspectable. However, BR-00 and BR-19-specific criteria are not encoded in the active files, so sufficiency vs replay is applied via generic chapter-family/ambiguity policy rather than BR-specific thresholds.","limitations":["BR-00/BR-19 behavior or acceptance criteria are out-of-bundle in the active slice, so family-level necessity cannot be proven directly from these files.","No replay execution artifacts are present in this runtime bundle; if BR-specific cases are behavior-critical, replay must be instantiated and judged in follow-on operational artifacts outside this snapshot."]}
