.md` reinforces that stronger operational language must be downgraded unless the required operational artifact floor exists. Because this scenario asks for a runtime-owned route decision rather than an executed replay verdict, no operator-only document is required and no stronger replay artifact must activate.","limitations":["BR-00 and BR-19 are not explicitly named in the active bundle, so the judgment maps them through the bundle's generic guide-reflection vs replay-escalation rules rather than family-specific runtime text.","Out-of-scope guide, benchmark, and replay documents were intentionally not consulted, so this verdict only assesses whether the active runtime bundle itself exposes the route."]}
