ion proof and that stronger operational artifacts activate only when benchmark/replay claims become operational or release-relevant. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` also makes the ladder explicit by showing `Guide reflection benchmark memo` as the document-grounded artifact with those replay artifacts as stronger siblings. `AGENTS.md` and the runtime guide both prefer the lightest sufficient path, so the bundle does not force unnecessary orchestration for this task.","limitations":["The active bundle does not explicitly define benchmark family IDs `BR-00` or `BR-19`; their mapping is inferred from the generic guide-reflection, benchmark-execution, and behavior-replay control surfaces.","No executed replay artifact is present in the active bundle, so this verdict confirms route exposure and artifact selection logic, not actual replay completion or replay-quality outcomes."]}
