raction, self-consistency-style comparison, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection, and it explicitly says prompt chaining remains anchored in base prompts. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` reinforces the boundary by saying advanced prompting and chaining examples are shape exemplars only and not policy owners. `grounded-research/SKILL.md` further carries decomposition, step-back, self-consistency-style comparison, and iterative/agentic retrieval into the active research skill surface. The bundle also avoids over-orchestration because `AGENTS.md` requires the lowest maturity surface that solves the task and bounds multi-agent use to cases where coordination materially improves the result.","limitations":["The active bundle does not explicitly tag BR-01, BR-14, BR-17, or BR-22 by benchmark ID; this verdict relies on explicit runtime-ownership language and technique coverage rather than a benchmark-labeled crosswalk."]}
