C:\WORK\0.ê°œì¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-c\EH-S01.stdout.log:1:{"scenario_id":"EH-S01","bundle_id":"eval_ops_reflection_bundle","verdict":"Partial Pass","guide_alignment":"partially_aligned","evidence_strength":"indirect","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/eval-ops/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md","prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_full.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md"],"answer_summary":"Document-level route is directly exposed as the primary path for guide reflection (`Guide reflection benchmark memo`), with explicit escalation to assembled-replay artifacts only when ambiguity/conflict or behavior-critical evidence needs stronger proof. The smallest ladder is: `Guide reflection benchmark memo` -> escalate to `Benchmark cohort manifest` -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`/`Replay suite verdict memo` only on trigger. For BR-00/BR-19, the active bundle does not force immediate replay activation by itself.","verdict_rationale":"The active runtime bundle clearly owns a document-first reflection workflow and defines escalation conditions and packet sequence for replay support. This gives a direct answer path for \"is document-level benchmark sufficient now?\" (yes, by default), but BR-00/BR-19-specific trigger determination is not resolved in-file; it depends on whether those family questions reveal ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims. The bundle therefore supports a partial, not fully final, family-specific decision.","limitations":["`BR-00` and `BR-19` definitions are outside the active bundle, so behavior-criticality cannot be decided from these files alone.","The result is routed by policy, not by in-scope family semantics.","No replay execution/runner state artifacts are present in this bundle, so any replay-grade claim would require those when triggered.","Evidence is policy-level (route ownership/exposure) rather than family-specific coverage scoring."]}
