C:\WORK\0.ê°œì¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-a\EH-S04.stderr.log:2827:{"scenario_id":"EH-S04","bundle_id":"coding_core_patch_bundle","verdict":"Pass","guide_alignment":"aligned","evidence_strength":"direct","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":true,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md","prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_standalone.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/coding-core/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md"],"answer_summary":"The active bundle gives a direct runtime-owned path: treat the stale owner sentence as a doc-to-runtime reflection gap, patch only the affected codex-layer sentence, verify with a guide-reflection route using `runtime_owner_check`, and escalate to replay artifacts only if the review surface moves from document parity to assembled replay.","verdict_rationale":"`coding-core`, `AGENTS.md`, and `PROMPT_standalone.md` all directly require narrow diffs, narrow change targets, verify-before-claim, and no speculative scope widening. `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay.md` reinforces `Narrow before widening`. `CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` directly says that if a chapter family can only be answered by operator-facing prose, that is a reflection gap and the actual prompt docs should be patched before claiming parity; it also maps guide/doc parity work to `Guide reflection benchmark memo` and only escalates to `Replay runner verdict sheet` / `Replay suite verdict memo` when the task has crossed into assembled replay or runner-state proof. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` gives direct verification structure for that route, including `runtime_owner_check`, anti-patterns against operator-only docs as runtime surfaces, and explicit rejection of stale ownership claims left alive after a patch round. The bundle also keeps multi-agent use bounded to genuine topology problems, so unnecessary orchestration is not indicated here.","limitations":["The active bundle justifies a sentence-scoped patch path and verification route, but it does not itself identify the exact stale sentence or exact target file; keeping `minimal_patch_targets` empty is the safest non-speculative reading.","No executed replay artifact is present in the bundle; replay packets are exposed only as escalation routes if the task shifts from document parity to assembled replay proof.","`CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` contains a packet-floor ownership reference to `PROMPT_guideline`, but that branch is not required for this narrow stale-owner-sentence fix path."]}
