C:\WORK\0.ê°œì¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-c\EH-S02.stderr.log:12951:C:\WORK\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\harness\runs\2026-05-06-a\EH-S02.stdout.log:1:{"scenario_id":"EH-S02","bundle_id":"grounded_research_appendix_bundle","verdict":"Pass","guide_alignment":"aligned","evidence_strength":"direct","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["C:\\WORK\\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\\PROMPT\\prompt-stack\\v32\\codex\\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","C:\\WORK\\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\\PROMPT\\prompt-stack\\v32\\01_base\\PROMPT_light.md","C:\\WORK\\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\\PROMPT\\prompt-stack\\v32\\02_overlays\\PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md","C:\\WORK\\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\\PROMPT\\prompt-stack\\v32\\03_examples\\PROMPT_example_catalog.md","C:\\WORK\\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\\PROMPT\\prompt-stack\\v32\\AGENTS.md","C:\\WORK\\0.ÃªÂ°Å“Ã¬ÂÂ¸\\PROMPT\\prompt-stack\\v32\\codex\\skills\\grounded-research\\SKILL.md"],"answer_summary":"The active bundle directly reflects both Prompt Chaining and Appendix A advanced prompting through runtime-owned files: chaining is owned by the base prompt, advanced prompting execution families are owned by the search-reasoning overlay, and the example catalog is explicitly non-owning shape support only.","verdict_rationale":"Pass. The runtime-owned answer path is explicit inside the active bundle. `CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` maps `Prompt Chaining / Planning` to the base prompts and maps `Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families` to `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`, while also stating that example-catalog references are structure-only and that operator-facing-only coverage would count as a reflection gap. `PROMPT_light.md` directly carries chaining behavior with explicit rules such as chaining only when staged dependency is real and only when it improves reliability. `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md` directly claims runtime ownership for advanced prompting execution families, including decomposition, step-back abstraction, self-consistency-style comparison, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection, and it explicitly says prompt chaining remains anchored in base prompts. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` reinforces the boundary by saying advanced prompting and chaining examples are shape exemplars only and not policy owners. `grounded-research/SKILL.md` further carries decomposition, step-back, self-consistency-style comparison, and iterative/agentic retrieval into the active research skill surface. The bundle also avoids over-orchestration because `AGENTS.md` requires the lowest maturity surface that solves the task and bounds multi-agent use to cases where coordination materially improves the result.","limitations":["The active bundle does not explicitly tag BR-01, BR-14, BR-17, or BR-22 by benchmark ID; this verdict relies on explicit runtime-ownership language and technique coverage rather than a benchmark-labeled crosswalk."]}
