322-### 3.1 Guide chapter-family quick lookup
323-
324-When Codex is maintaining reflection against a governing guide, use these anchor routes:
325-
326-- Prompt Chaining / Planning -> base prompts; keep staged dependency, checkpoint, and fallback visibility explicit instead of collapsing into one-shot execution language
327-- Routing / Prioritization / Exploration -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo` or `Prioritization queue / next-action memo`
328-- Parallelization / Multi-Agent / A2A -> `PROMPT_multi_agent_overlay` + `orchestration-control`; prefer `Delegation admission memo`, `A2A task-handoff memo`, and `Join-quality review memo`
329-- Tool Use / MCP -> `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay`; prefer `Tool capability contract / precondition memo` or `MCP capability handoff memo`
330-- Memory / Learning / Adaptation -> `PROMPT_memory_adaptation_overlay`; prefer `Memory scope / checkpoint profile memo`, `Learning-signal review memo`, and `Adaptation decision memo`
331-- Goal / Monitoring / Recovery / HITL -> base prompts; prefer `Goal-monitoring status memo`, `Recovery / escalation checkpoint memo`, and `HITL approval packet`
332-- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
333-- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
334-- Reasoning Techniques / Reflection -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Critique quality review memo` when critique utility or no-gain loops are under review
335-- Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay` for decomposition, step-back, self-consistency, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection; keep prompt chaining in base prompts and treat example-catalog references as structure-only
336-- Guardrails / Safety -> `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay`
337:- Evaluation / Monitoring -> `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay` + `eval-ops`; prefer `Benchmark registry memo`, `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, or `Prompt-stack release review`
338-
339-Lookup rule:
340-- if a chapter family can only be answered by operator-facing prose and not by the active runtime / skill surface, treat that as a reflection gap and patch the actual prompt docs before claiming parity
341-
342-Packet rule:
343-- one packet should solve one control problem
344-- if packet overhead exceeds its decision value, simplify or drop it
345-- if a task family has a required packet floor, do not silently downgrade it to an optional convenience note
346-- `PROMPT_guideline` direct packet floor matrix owns first-pass `required / recommended / optional packet` decisions; `Packet compliance report` audits observed-vs-required coverage, omission findings, and claim downgrades against that floor
347-- if the required packet exists but the recommended companion is missing, keep the narrower companion-missing language rather than full-strength claim language
348-- if future behavior or reusable defaults are being changed, pair `Learning-signal review memo` with `Adaptation decision memo` rather than silently mutating defaults
349-- if async or delegated work remains active, prefer lifecycle packets over prose-only status narration
350-- host-runtime maintenance and release reviews should still be able to see whether packet families cover the active control boundaries
351-- keep guide / runtime / skill lookup parity visible for goal, recovery, approval, budget, prioritization, readiness, and lifecycle-audit packets; do not let one layer silently know a family the others no longer expose
352-- keep coding-briefing, research-transparency, resource-concurrency, packet-compliance, replay-review, release-evidence, benchmark-registry, context-sufficiency, critique-quality, adaptation-promotion, and route-quality packets equally visible when those are the live control boundaries
353-- keep benchmark-execution, replay-verdict, context-failure, critique-utility, adaptation-lifecycle, route-reprioritization, coding-proof, release-v2, and telemetry-trend packets equally visible when those are the live control boundaries
354-- packet presence is not operational proof; if execution, controller behavior, or promotion evidence is the live question, choose the artifact that actually carries the linked evidence
355-- distinguish `light review memo`, `stronger packet`, and `operational artifact` rather than treating every packet as equal-strength evidence
356-- if a lighter memo and a stronger artifact address the same control problem, keep the stronger artifact active and background or supersede the lighter memo
357-- if the task has crossed from packet presence review into operational proof review, prefer the stronger operational artifact and mark weaker packets as superseded rather than silently doubling them
